// Kernels refer to variables by NAME (Fig. 2: [[x := E]]p = sigma_p[x |-> [[E]]p]).
// y's kernel is delta(x + 1) with dep {x}.  Reassigning x afterwards is
// allowed by the assumption (the new kernel of x has no dependencies), but
// it also changes the joint measure seen through y: E[y] becomes 3 + 1 = 4,
// whereas in an ordinary (sampling) execution y would keep mean 0 + 1 = 1.
x ~ Normal(0, 1)
y := x + 1
query mean(y)            // 1
x := 3
query mean(y)            // 4 under the kernel-based semantics
